# Sensitive Clinical Bridge — Canonical User Identity

## Rule
All Sensitive Clinical Bridge persistence, audit, and orchestrator code MUST use `users.username` as the canonical user_id.

## Boundary resolution
The chat path passes hardware_id. At the bridge boundary (therapeutic_controller.prepare_therapeutic_context), call:
  from app.services._identity_resolver import resolve_username
  canonical_user_id = await resolve_username(db_pool, user_id)

Then pass canonical_user_id (NOT the original user_id) to evaluate_disclosure and all downstream consumers.

## Forbidden patterns
- Querying sensitive_bridge_enrollment, user_safety_codewords, user_trigger_dates, user_polyvictimization_layers, user_legal_status, sensitive_bridge_log by hardware_id
- Querying user_parts_registry, addiction_status_history, or cross_addiction_transfer_events by hardware_id
- Querying v1.4 JSONB subkeys by hardware_id: sex_addiction_status, gambling_status, gaming_status, food_compulsion_status, work_compulsion_status, spending_compulsion_status, codependency_status, cross_addiction_profile, sensitive_clinical
- Adding new tables with FK to users(hardware_id) for Sensitive Bridge surfaces
- Special-casing identity per cohort, user, or session

## Why
Schema FKs (migrations 202-207) reference users(username). Pre-resolution chat path passed hardware_id, causing orchestrator to return empty data even when enrollment existed. Fixed in commit a7c03b7 (Priority 1).
